# Companion Document — CMS05 Design Spec

The latest CMS05 design document remains the detailed authority for the output-cache design.

The handover documents do not need to duplicate every CMS05 detail. They must, however, identify which CMS05 decisions are already implemented, which are pending, and which are deferred.

When a new chat is asked to modify output-cache code, upload CMS05 with the handover pack.

The new chat should be instructed:

```text
Use CMS05 as the detailed design reference.
Use the current session handover as the current implementation-state authority.
Use the decision log to avoid re-opening settled decisions.
If CMS05 and current code appear to conflict, stop and ask for clarification
rather than guessing.
```

