# Maintenance Rules for the Handover Pack

## Updating Document A

Update only when:

* project-wide rules change;
* coding/comment/update rules change;
* a major environment or architecture rule changes.

Do not update Document A for every phase.

## Updating Document B

Update when:

* a major decision is made;
* a previously deferred approach becomes accepted or rejected;
* an old decision is superseded.

Do not use the decision log as a session diary.

## Updating Document C

Update at every chat/session boundary.

It must always contain:

* current phase;
* last completed phase;
* immediate next task;
* latest meaningful test evidence;
* do-not-implement list;
* files likely needed.

Document C is the most volatile document and should be treated as the current-state authority.

